{% extends "shell.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ copy.overview_title }} · {{ copy.product }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{#
  `RCA-005` FR-120: latest work, data state, and items needing attention, drawn from rows the
  specification retains. Blueprint §7.1 calls this operational orientation, not analytics.

  Nothing here is a figure. No count, no chart, no total -- `M3-U5` forbids them by name and
  `test_overview_carries_no_figure` asserts the rendered text has no digit outside `<time>`. The
  rows arrive shaped from `shell_workspace.py`; this template decides nothing about them, and the
  scan in `test_no_shell_template_computes` holds it to that.

  **Composition (`RCA-010` §Scope, handoff §4 screen 01).** The same regions the read model has
  always carried, recomposed rather than extended: a raised page header holding the title, the lede
  and the one dominant action; the attention callout when there is something to attend to; then a
  module grid -- latest work, anything still processing, data, pinned, and recent. The handoff's KPI
  strip is absent because `read_overview` carries no figure for it (handoff §4: "omit it and
  report -- do not invent it").

  Modules are `div`s with an `h2`, not labelled `section`s: they are regions of one surface, and a
  landmark per module would add five navigation stops the surface did not have.
#}
<section class="workspace-page" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  {#
    `RCA-012` `FR-212` and `U1` slice 12: the approved hero artwork, with the page head on it.

    The handoff's own composition (§6, §10): the title, lede and the one action sit on the band
    over an ivory wash, inside its solid stop, with the artwork showing on the trailing side. The
    band is inside the labelled region so `aria-labelledby` resolves within it. The artwork states
    no figure, population, refusal or state (`FR-218`), and the copy lives outside `<picture>`, so a
    reader whose image never loads keeps a complete, legible surface on the band's ground colour.
    The `alt` comes from the copy module; the wash is `aria-hidden` presentation.

    `eager` and `fetchpriority="high"` because it is above the fold. The WebP source is listed first
    so a browser that supports it takes the smaller file; the JPEG is the `<img>` fallback.
  #}
  <div class="hero-band">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="{{ assets }}/khepri-hero.webp" type="image/webp">
      <img class="hero-band__image"
           src="{{ assets }}/khepri-hero.jpg"
           alt="{{ copy.overview_hero_alt }}"
           loading="eager"
           fetchpriority="high">
    </picture>
    <div class="hero-band__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="page-head page-head--hero page-head--display">
    <div class="page-head__text">
      <h1 id="page-title">{{ copy.overview_title }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{{ copy.overview_intro }}</p>
    </div>
    {#
      The one dominant action (§7.1), posting to `R8-06`'s route exactly as the chooser's active
      row does. Offered only when a bridge is wired: a form whose every submission the shell
      refuses reads as a fault, not as a capability nobody installed.
    #}
    {% if bridge_available %}
    <form class="page-head__actions" method="post" action="{{ prefix }}/{{ language }}/{{ organization_id }}/analyses">
      <button class="button--primary" type="submit">{{ copy.new_analysis }}</button>
    </form>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  </div>

  {#
    Rendered only when non-empty, and first: an always-present "no issues" panel is decoration,
    not reassurance (§7.1), and a failure the reader must act on outranks orientation.
  #}
  {% if view.attention %}
  <div class="module module--attention">
    <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.attention_title }}</h2>
    <ul class="attention-list">
      {% for item in view.attention %}
      <li class="attention-item">
        <span>{{ copy.attention_run_failed }}</span>
        <time datetime="{{ item.started.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ item.started.text }}</time>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="module-grid">
    <div class="module">
      <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.latest_work_title }}</h2>
      {% if view.latest_work %}
      <p class="latest-work">
        <span class="row-state">{{ copy[view.latest_work.state_key] }}</span>
        <time datetime="{{ view.latest_work.started.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ view.latest_work.started.text }}</time>
      </p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="empty-state">{{ copy.overview_no_work }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {#
      Everything still running, so a run that started before a newer one finished is not lost
      behind "latest work" (§7.1: is anything processing?). Rendered only when non-empty.
    #}
    {% if view.processing %}
    <div class="module">
      <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.processing_title }}</h2>
      <ul class="processing-list">
        {% for item in view.processing %}
        <li class="processing-item">
          <span class="row-state">{{ copy[item.state_key] }}</span>
          <time datetime="{{ item.started.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ item.started.text }}</time>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="module">
      <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.data_title }}</h2>
      {% if view.latest_data %}
      <p class="latest-data">
        <span class="row-state">{{ copy[view.latest_data.admission_key] }}</span>
        <span class="row-state">{{ copy[view.latest_data.readiness_key] }}</span>
        <time datetime="{{ view.latest_data.submitted.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ view.latest_data.submitted.text }}</time>
      </p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="empty-state">{{ copy.overview_no_data }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {#
      `W1-09` (`FR-128`/`FR-129`), under active `KHEPRI-DEC-034`.

      Both regions render whether or not they hold rows, unlike attention: an empty "Pinned" tells a
      reader the capability exists and how to use it, where an empty "no issues" panel would be
      reassurance nobody asked for (§7.1).

      **No count anywhere.** `KHEPRI-DEC-034` §2 refuses counting and ranking, and
      `test_overview_carries_no_figure` asserts the rendered text holds no digit outside a
      `<time>`. Order is carried by the list, never numbered. Neither region says anything about
      expiry: the retention notice below is the one place this surface speaks about retention.
    #}
    <div class="module">
      <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.pinned_title }}</h2>
      {% if view.pinned %}
      <ul class="pinned-list">
        {% for item in view.pinned %}
        <li class="pinned-item">
          <span class="row-state">{{ copy[item.kind_key] }}</span>
          <time datetime="{{ item.at.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ item.at.text }}</time>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% else %}
      <p class="empty-state">{{ copy.pinned_empty }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="module module--wide">
      <h2 class="module__title">{{ copy.recent_title }}</h2>
      {% if view.recent %}
      <ul class="recent-list">
        {% for item in view.recent %}
        <li class="recent-item">
          <span class="row-state">{{ copy[item.kind_key] }}</span>
          <time datetime="{{ item.at.at }}" dir="ltr">{{ item.at.text }}</time>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% else %}
      <p class="empty-state">{{ copy.recent_empty }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {#
    `KHEPRI-DEC-033` §5: until `W1-07` ships the sweep, no surface may say content expires
    automatically. This states what is true of the store today and claims nothing about a purge.
  #}
  <p class="retention-notice">{{ copy.retention_notice }}</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
